          <dt pn="section-1.4-4.5">Secondary-NBNS-Address</dt>
          <dd pn="section-1.4-4.6">The four octet Secondary-NBNS-Address is the address of the
secondary NBNS server to be used by the local peer.  If all
four octets are set to zero, it indicates an explicit request
that the peer provide the address information in a Config-Nak
packet.</dd>
          <dt pn="section-1.4-4.7">Default</dt>
          <dd pn="section-1.4-4.8">No address is provided.</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>
